        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnny Edwards, Ian Anderson, Jennie Franks\n- Bands: Buster Brown, Montrose, King Kobra, Wild Horses, Northrup, Royal Jelly, Foreigner, Jethro Tull\n- Roles: rock singer, lead singer, lead vocalist, flautist, acoustic guitarist, songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, wife\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Scott Anderson was born on 10 August 1947 and is a Scottish-born musician, singer, songwriter, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- From 1970 to 1974, Jennie Franks was the first wife of Ian Anderson.\n- Johnny Edwards is an American rock singer who sang for Buster Brown, Montrose, King Kobra, Wild Horses, Northrup, and Royal Jelly.\n- Johnny Edwards is best known as the second lead singer of Foreigner.\n- Ian Anderson is best known for his work as the lead vocalist, flautist, and acoustic guitarist of Jethro Tull.",
